title: 'Anthropic, "Effective context engineering for AI agents" (2025): the smallest set of high-signal tokens, at the right altitude, with notes kept outside the context.'
pid: 92d8134c-00fb-4259-8eb3-fd2b265134fe
body: |2-
  https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents
  Between brittle rules and vague guidance is the "right altitude".
  Long work survives by compaction, by notes the agent writes and
  rereads, or by subagents that return a condensed summary. Load
  references just in time rather than all at once. Our graph is the
  note-taking kind; the request barrier of the home note is its altitude.
